title: Prefab copies stay linked
intro: Placed copies remember their prefab. Change one, save it, and every copy in every scene follows.
project: Platformer | Prefab Links

chapter: Make a prefab | Entity > Save as Prefab
look: 8, -2, 4
deselect
create: Sprite
rename: Gem
set: Transform.Position = 5, -3, 0
set: Sprite.Tint = #29ADFF
set: Sprite.Size = 0.6, 0.6
add: Pickup
say: Here's a gem worth one point. We want lots of them through the level, all alike.
menu: Entity > Save as Prefab
expectfile: Prefabs/Gem.prefab
expectprefab: Gem = Gem
explain: prefab:Gem | A prefab copy | Saving it as a prefab makes the gem a copy of the new prefab. The Hierarchy marks copies with a package.
explain: prefabnote | Copy of the Gem prefab | And the Inspector says which prefab it's a copy of.

chapter: Place copies | Duplicate, or drag the prefab in from Assets
key: Ctrl+D
rename: Gem 2
set: Transform.Position = 7.5, -3, 0
key: Ctrl+D
rename: Gem 3
set: Transform.Position = 11, -3, 0
expectprefab: Gem 2 = Gem
expectprefab: Gem 3 = Gem
explain: world:4, -1.5, 12, -4.2 | Three copies | Duplicating a copy keeps the link, and so does dragging the prefab in from the Assets panel. Each copy has its own name and place.

chapter: Change one, update them all | Save as Prefab on a copy
select: Gem 2
set: Sprite.Tint = #FF004D
set: Sprite.Size = 0.9, 0.9
set: Pickup.Amount = 5
say: Say gems should be red, bigger and worth five. We change just one of them.
menu: Entity > Save as Prefab
say: Saving a copy saves over its own prefab, whatever the copy is called. Griff checks first, since every copy will change.
answer: Yes
expectvalue: Gem.Sprite.Tint = #FF004D
expectvalue: Gem 3.Pickup.Amount = 5
expectat: Gem 3 = 11, -3
explain: world:4, -1.5, 12, -4.2 | Every copy updated | The other copies take the prefab's new look and value straight away, and stay where they were placed. Copies in other scenes are updated in their files too.
key: Ctrl+Z
expectvalue: Gem 3.Sprite.Tint = #29ADFF
say: In this scene it's one step to undo.
key: Ctrl+Y
expectvalue: Gem 3.Sprite.Tint = #FF004D

chapter: Unlink a copy | Entity > Unlink from Prefab
select: Gem 3
menu: Entity > Unlink from Prefab
expectprefab: Gem 3 = none
say: To keep one copy as it is, unlink it. It becomes an ordinary entity, and saving the prefab leaves it alone.
